There are two data types
1.Primitive(call by value)(string,null,Number,Boolean,Undefined,Symbol,BigInt)
const num=12.7
const mm=null//case sensitive
const person;
const sex=Symbol("145")//symbol is used to create different datatypes for unique id's
const gender=Symbol("145")
console.log(sex===gender)//results false
const npsf=12233654789556956985n//n convert number to BigInt

2.Non-Primitive(reference type)(array,Objects,Functions)
const fruits=["aam",'kela',"amrud","santra","sev"]
Objects
let Obj={name:"kush",age:20}
const fum=function(){console.log("Hello")}
null ka typeof se data object aata hai

saare non primitive ka data type function hot ahai aur funtion ka object funtion hota hai
 
Stack (Primitive)---copy,Heap(Non-Primitive)---reference









